  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Decide whether these functions are odd, even, or neither.\n\nYou may need to use $|-x|=|x|$ and $|x-y|=|y-x|$. Check your answers using DESMOS.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x|+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|-x|+1\\\\&=|x|+1\\\\&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f$ is even. Its graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x|+x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(1)&=|1|+1=2,\\\\f(-1)&=|-1|-1=0.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $f(-1)\\ne f(1)$ and $f(-1)\\ne-f(1)$, $f$ is neither even nor odd. Its graph has neither $y$-axis symmetry nor origin symmetry.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x\\times|x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)|-x|\\\\&=-x|x|\\\\&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f$ is odd. Its graph is symmetric about the origin.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x^3+x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|(-x)^3+(-x)|\\\\&=|-x^3-x|\\\\&=|-(x^3+x)|\\\\&=|x^3+x|\\\\&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f$ is even. Its graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{|x|-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ge0$, $|x|-x=0$, so the function is undefined. For $x<0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\frac{x}{-x-x}\\\\&=\\frac{x}{-2x}\\\\&=-\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $(-\\infty,0)$, which is not symmetric about zero, so $f$ is neither even nor odd. Its graph is the horizontal ray $y=-\\tfrac12$ for $x<0$, with neither required symmetry.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x-1|+|x+1|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=|-x-1|+|-x+1|\\\\&=|-(x+1)|+|-(x-1)|\\\\&=|x+1|+|x-1|\\\\&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f$ is even. Its graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
